{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/276491-new-storyteller-seeks-advice","id":276491,"title":"New Storyteller seeks Advice!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-09T11:01:03-07:00","id":276491,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> New Storyteller seeks Advice!","content":"Hello everybody!<br /> <br /> I'm a new Storyteller living in S\u00e3o Paulo - Brazil, and I'll be starting a new Werewolf The Forsaken game this weekend. I've read through the entire World of Darkness and Werewolf The Forsaken rulebooks; and I'm confident I got what it takes to be the Storyteller to our troupe.<br /> Nonethless, it's always good to have other (and more experienced) Storytellers' advices.<br /> What do you have to tell me that you think would be usefull for a first timer?<br /> <br /> Thank you all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4038-leopaiva","name":"LeoPaiva","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4038_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T12:36:56-07:00","id":276576,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...<br /> <br /> First thing I would establish is that a good ST's number one priority is facilitating fun for the group This shouldn't have to be said, but I think it bears mentioning all the time anyway, because it is so easily forgotten, especially once you get into crafting the story and setting for your game. I won't dictate how you do this for your players; some would say &quot;let your players make decisions, empower them, etc.&quot;, but personally, that's not how it works for my group, so I utilize a combination of letting them exercise free will as well as manipulating them towards particular story-progressing decisions, because story progression is something we find enjoyable. You'll have to see what works for your group (unless you've already figured it out, in which case, hooray!)<br /> <br /> That aside, the second most important thing for me is figuring out the story you want to tell. The default premise for Werewolf is that of a sandbox game, where you give your players a setting (territory), and they interact with it. But that really only works with players who are not only immersed in their characters but are also proactive by nature. Thankfully, Werewolf allows for the crafting of other stories as well: your players can go on fantasy-esque adventures in the Spirit World, where you can easily fit epic landscapes, spirits can play the role of monsters, potential allies, or quirky scenery, and fetishes take the narrative place of magical artifacts and relics. Or their pack could be drafted into a Silver Crusade, large-scale war of Forsaken vs. Pure, and that could be the stage for war horror, political intrigue, and deeds of epic bravery.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you should go for what you and your group would enjoy.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, and this is what will take up most of your time as an ST, actually, even more than the time you spend actually running your game: Setting. This not only includes the place/s that your story will be staged in, but also the NPCs - both in the Flesh and Spirit world - and their relationships and interactions. The more you write beforehand, the more you are ready for what happens during the game itself; not only that, but I find that the more detail you pack into your setting, the meatier it becomes, and then your players just have more to sink their teeth into (see what I did there?). Give your players all sorts of potential allies friends, love interests, people to hate, people to fight, people to kill, heck, people to ignore.<br /> <br /> It's hard work, of course, and not everyone will be able to appreciate it; not everyone will even be able to notice it. But as a gamer myself, I've always found that the best games were the ones who gave you all sorts of toys (powers, items, NPCs), let you play with them, and let you deal with the consequences afterward. This has always been the draw of tabletop games for me.<br /> <br /> Fourth most important is letting your players just... play. Let them have goals and pursue them. Let each of their characters have lives. In the last Forsaken game I ran back in 2011, I had 5 players, all good friends of mine and each other. I immediately knew that one of my problems would be fostering their individual goals while still maintaining narrative cohesion (i.e., the story still makes sense even though there are 5 main characters and they are all taking up screentime). What I did was implement a basic Aspirations system for my players: before we start a game session or right after finishing one, they had to write 3 things that they would want to happen to their characters, or have their characters do, in the next session. In this way, I was able to write the &quot;main storyline&quot; for each session while injecting little details here and there that would help my players fulfill their Aspirations. For example, one of the Rahu players wrote &quot;I want to do something heroic&quot;, so I introduced a damsel in distress for him to encounter at a random point in the game (while he was exploring the pack's new territory).<br /> <br /> Well, this has been a much longer post than I thought it would be, but I hope it helps, and good luck with your game! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 10-09-2014, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T14:10:34-07:00","id":276627,"title":"","content":"Recommended reading:<br /> <b>Lore of the Forsaken</b> - for all the goodies about spirit magics and the Tribal Totems<br /> <b>The Rage</b> - for all the details on being a member of the Tribes of the Moon<br /> <b>Predators </b>- for all the spirits and how they might look &amp; act, etc.<br /> <b>Blood of the Wolf </b>- for all the nitty gritty of being a shape-shifting half-wolf<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T15:05:46-07:00","id":276683,"title":"","content":"The 'Lodges' books give some more options to your players if they're interested in joining one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:49:54-07:00","id":276806,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go with something simple to add to the already great advice here: start with the basics. <br /> <br /> I've seen new Werewolf ST's attempt to bring in something odd or strange, something outside of the &quot;usual suspects&quot; (the Pure, the Hosts, etc) that would surprise the players. The game was alright, but it wasn't - in my opinion, anyway - as good as it could have been. So start small, keep things in the core book for now, and add as you feel comfortable. Unless you're experienced enough in general to do it, don't jump into the deep end and feel like you need to include everything. Start with what your group is comfortable starting with, and build from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T04:28:30-07:00","id":277098,"title":"","content":"Thank you Ursufgutha Storm-Born and strider1276 for the great advice!<br /> <br /> I'll try to keep it simple, and focus the story on the characters first contacts with the Uratha Society.<br /> <br /> They will all be playing young werewolves that have recently gone thorugh their first change, so much like the players themselves, the characters will be new to the whole werewolf universe (that should encourage them to roleplay the confusion they are going through).<br /> <br /> Once again thak you for your help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4038-leopaiva","name":"LeoPaiva","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4038_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T05:21:41-07:00","id":277116,"title":"","content":"Bit of advice, READ the storytelling section in the core book. Then read it again. There's good stuff in there that always gets forgotten. Watch a variety of werewolf films as well to draw inspiration. Wer is currently out, check that one and American werewolf in London for fun. Dog soldiers is another good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T09:58:49-07:00","id":277329,"title":"","content":"I'll do that Lyrics Of War. I've read it twice by now, but I'll keep reading it so the information is always on my mind!<br /> <br /> Thank you very much!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4038-leopaiva","name":"LeoPaiva","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4038_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T15:29:39-07:00","id":277598,"title":"","content":"another thing, storytellers handbook revised from werewolf the apocalypse. Good stuff, even if it applies to cwod mostly. Speaking of, should be getting my wyrm pdf soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:25:55-07:00","id":279655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/276491-new-storyteller-seeks-advice?p=277116#post277116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of advice, READ the storytelling section in the core book. Then read it again. There's good stuff in there that always gets forgotten. Watch a variety of werewolf films as well to draw inspiration. Wer is currently out, check that one and American werewolf in London for fun. Dog soldiers is another good one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then read it AGAIN! Most under-used part of the corebooks in general and (seems to be) REALLY under-used for Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}